AlphaServer 1000 4/200 System

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides the features users demand of a workgroup server or small
   business server running database, PC LAN, Internet access,
   communications, or other business-critical applications

o  Offers leadership price/performance for under $18,000 -- bringing the
   power and robustness of AlphaServer systems to low-end commercial and
   technical computing users

o  Available in November on Windows NT and OpenVMS AXP platforms and soon on
   DEC OSF/1

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaServer 1000 4/200 system is a 200 MHz Alpha uni-processor server in
a deskside tower enclosure running DEC OSF/1, OpenVMS AXP, or Windows NT
software. It offers high reliability features, such as fully redundant power
supplies, internal RAID, hot swap disk, dual SCSI backplane, ECC memory, and
ECC cache.

This product offers server management features such as heat, fan failure,
and power supply sensors. Remote management can be handled via a simple
serial link. The system includes an LCD operator control panel.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/200 provides for up to 10 internal mass storage
devices, which include a floppy diskette drive and a CD-ROM. The server also
supports up to 512 Mbytes of RAM memory and over 14 Gbytes of internal disk
storage, along with provision for a tape drive, support for wide SCSI
devices, and up to seven hot swap StorageWorks disk drives.

Integrated on the system motherboard are:

o  Industry standard SVGA controller
o  Floppy disk controller
o  Two serial ports and one parallel port
o  Keyboard and mouse controller
o  LCD operator control panel

BENEFITS

The reliability features, combined with simple management features, make the
AlphaServer 1000 ideal for organizations with little or no MIS support.
Business-critical applications can run unattended; management features
provide early indications of potential system failures.

Remote diagnosis allows system administrators to call in, remotely run the
diagnostics, configure the system, and recommend a fix or pull the right
part. Support costs are minimized because on-site visits and service calls
are minimized.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/200 provides large system features and performance at
small system prices. With its daughter card CPU architecture, and design for
compatibility with future generations of Alpha chips, the server is easily
upgraded for higher performance. And for even greater investment protection,
users have a choice of three popular operating systems: DEC OSF/1, OpenVMS
AXP, or Windows NT platforms.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The AlphaServer 1000 4/200 systems running Windows NT Server and OpenVMS
V6.1-1H2 will be available in November. The version running DEC OSF/1 V3.0b
will be available in December. All of the options listed will be supported
on the ship date.

