   exceed $130 per square foot. A dual host AlphaServer 2100 4/275 CAB
   system requires half the space of a comparable pedestal configuration
   while providing more storage capability.

o  Serviceability -- The rackmount unit is mounted on slides for easy access
   to all necessary components, minimizing down time during service. The
   AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM also has a shock and vibration rating that is
   twice the industry standard. This gives the AlphaServer 4/275 RM a much
   higher survival rate during earthquakes or other similar situations.

o  Designed with high availability in mind -- To provide the highest level
   of availability, the AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM was designed with minimal
   internal storage. This feature allows for the creation of high
   availability configurations independent of the storage, providing hot
   swappable disks and power supplies for the BA350s. For the highest level
   of availability, all storage (including removables) could be located in
   StorageWorks shelves to provide hot swapability.

o  Highly available power systems -- The AlphaServer 2100 4/275 RM supports
   optional fully redundant power supplies in a N+1 arrangement allowing a
   single power supply to support a fully loaded system. Other high
   availability features available with packaged systems include: dual AC
   power controllers, optional rackmounted UPS systems, and redundant power
   supplies for the StorageWorks shelves.

