DEC 7000 Model 700 -- Highest Capacity, Most Scalable Server

HIGHLIGHTS

o  The industry's leadership performance enterprise server, boasting the
   highest AIM performance rating ever recorded -- 643.5!

o  Industry leader in customer investment protection

o  Features and performance for commercial UNIX and OpenVMS users

o  Simplified ordering via Base Enterprise Server offerings and Enterprise
   Expansion Packages

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

A follow-on to the existing DEC 7000 Model 600, the DEC 7000 Model 700 is
Digital's highest performing, most expandable server. It incorporates the
world's fastest microprocessor, the 275-MHz DECchip 21064A, which is based
on the Alpha 64-bit architecture.

BENEFITS

The DEC 7000 Model 700 provides IT managers with an enterprise server
designed to give their clients an unprecedented response time in transaction
processing, database access, simulations, and file serving. With the
industry's best price/performance and superior expansion and upgrade
capabilities, the DEC 7000 Model 700 ensures users' investment protection.

Because the DEC 7000 is based on the 64-bit Alpha architecture, it has the
capacity to take users into the next century while solving their most
challenging business problems today. Large physical and virtual memory
provide significant increases, over traditional 32-bit systems, in the
performance of database and technical applications. Support for large files
(up to 32 Gbytes) and file systems that enterprises require are now possible
with the DEC 7000. With this support, users gain the comfort of knowing that
their applications can grow as their business grows, without needing
re-design. And implementing new technologies such as multimedia and
object-oriented applications can be accommodated easily.

Users can upgrade the DEC 7000 Model 600 to the DEC 7000 Model 700 by simply
replacing the Model 600 CPU Module with a Model 700 CPU Module. That's it --
the power, packaging, cooling, memory, I/O, and options remain the same. The
rules are the same when upgrading from VAX 7000 machines to the DEC 7000
Model 700, with the exception of the DSSI disk/tape controller; the DSSI
controller for the DEC 7000 is the KFMSB-AA.

Also, DEC 7000 owners will be able to upgrade to future product offerings in
cabinet enclosures. The message is simple: No matter when, which technology,
or operating system you purchase first within Digital's Enterprise Server
line, you can upgrade to the latest technology without the large expense and
disruption of replacing the entire platform. The DEC 7000 is truly a
timeless system platform.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DEC 7000 Model 700 is shipping now with a 15 day leadtime. It is
available through Digital's sales offices and business partners.

The DEC 7000 Model 700 is on the 'Q' software tier.

Packaging

The DEC 7000 Model 700 offerings are simple and flexible. Offered as Base
Enterprise Server configurations, they include:

o  DEC 7000 Model 700 CPU module
o  275 MHz DECchip 21064A -- 16 Kbytes of on-chip instruction cache, 16
   Kbytes of on-chip data cache, and 4 Mbytes of on-board cache
o  Choice of 128, 256, 512, or 2,048 Mbytes of memory
o  KZMSA Fast SCSI-2 disk or tape controller
o  DEMNA XMI to Ethernet adapter
o  RRD43 in-cabinet CD-ROM reader
o  12 Slot XMI backplance
o  Choice of DEC OSF/1 or OpenVMS AXP base operating system license
o  NAS 200 license

Additionally, Digital is now offering Enterprise Expansion Packages that
turn these base servers into either OpenVMS cluster starter systems, OpenVMS
cluster add-on systems, or highly available DEC OSF/1 systems. These
Enterprise Expansion Packages are specifically designed to create fully
functional systems when they are added to Base Enterprise Server offerings.
They contain all the necessary hardware, except for the console terminal,
and software to provide a complete, operational system.

The Expansion Packages

o  DEC OSF/1 High Availability SCSI Package (-DA/DB order number):
   SW800 StorageWorks cabinet with HSZ40 StorageWorks array controller in
   BA350-MB, six 2.1 Gbyte RZ28, 3.5-inch disk drives in BA350 shelf, 20
   Gbyte TZ87, 5.25-inch SCSI tape drive in BA350 shelf, BN21K 10-meter
   cable and DWZZA for connecting HSZ40 to KZMSA in system cabinet, and
   DECsafe Available Server software license kit.

o  OpenVMS AXP Cluster Starter Package (-AA/AB order number):
   SW800 StorageWorks cabinet with HSJ40 StorageWorks array controller in
   BA350-MB, six 2.1 Gbyte RZ28, 3.5-inch disk drives in BA350 shelf, 20
   Gbyte TZ87, 5.25-inch SCSI tape drive in BA350 shelf, CIXCD-AC XMI CI
   controller, and VMScluster license. Resides in XMI slot in system
   cabinet, connects to HSJ40 in SW800 via BNCIA 10-meter cable to SC008, to
   second BNCIA 10-meter cable, to HSJ40.

o  OpenVMS AXP Cluster Add-on Package (-AX order number):
   CIXCD-AC XMI CI controller, BNCIA-10 2 CI 10-meter cable, and VMScluster
   license.

NOTE: When adding additional storage devices to SW800, the necessary BA350
      shelves must be ordered.

To further simplify, Digital will not be offering a preconfigured DEC 10000
package. However, users retain the flexibility to build their DEC 7000 up to
DEC 10000 functionality. The battery cabinet (H9B00-AF), not previously
orderable, can now be purchased and added to the DEC 7000. Additionally, by
adding two power regulators to the DEC 7000, users will have the highly
reliable and available features that the DEC 10000 offered.

Upgrades

Upgrading to a DEC 7000 Model 700 is now achieved as follows:

o  To add additional CPU boards to a DEC 7000 Model 710 base server:
   - Order part number 7KATA-MK for OpenVMS AXP systems or 7KATA-NK for DEC
   OSF/1 systems. This number contains one DEC 7000 Model 700 CPU module
   plus an SMP license. Up to five additional kits can be ordered.

o  To upgrade from a VAX 7000-6xx/7xx, VAX 10000-6xX/7xx, DEC 7000-6xx, or
   DEC 10000-6xx:
   - Replace the first CPU module by ordering part number 7KAVA-FC for
     OpenVMS AXP systems and 7KAVA-DC for DEC OSF/1 systems. This number
     contains a DEC 7000 Model 700 CPU module plus a base operating system
     license, and requires the return of the CPU module being traded.
   - Then order 7KAVA-MC for OpenVMS AXP and 7KAVA-NC for DEC OSF/1 systems
   for each additional CPU and SMP license required. These part numbers
   require the return of one CPU per each one ordered.

