warranty; with nine-hour per day, five-day per week coverage; and a four-
hour response time.

TECHNICAL DATA

DEC 7000 Model 700 requires OpenVMS AXP V6.1 or DEC OSF/1 V3.0 for UNIX
users. Additional DEC 7000 Model 700 features include:

o  Ability to connect to over 7 Tbytes of data on DEC OSF/1 machines through
   support for the HSZ40 and increased SCSI channel support; each HSZ40
   supports up to 42 disks (2.1 Gbyte, 3.5-inch RZ28-VA), 6 HSZ40s per SCSI
   channel, and up to 32 SCSI channels.

o  Support for high availability features:
   - OpenVMS Clusters, via the CI interconnect (the CIXCD-AC) and, now, via
     the DSSI for Alpha interconnect (the KFMSB-AA), which has been shipping
     since mid-May and is supported by OpenVMS AXP V6.1.
   - High availability features over the SCSI bus provided by the DECsafe
     ASE layered product, which is now supported on DEC OSF/1 systems.
   - Hot swap of disk drives.
   - RAID 0 support, via the HSZ40 Flexible Interconnect Bus on DEC OSF/1
     and via the HSJ40 on OpenVMS AXP systems.
   - RAID 5 support, via the HSZ40 Flexible Interconnect Bus.
   - Support for software based shadowing and striping on DEC OSF/1 based
     systems via the Logical Storage Manager (LSM) layered product.
   - Redundant power features and capabilities.

