Warranty & Service Offerings for AlphaStation/AlphaServer Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Digital has established a three-year warranty standard

o  All bundled software products (operating system and NAS) now carry
   consistent levels of warranty

SERVICE DESCRIPTION

With the announcement of the AlphaStation and AlphaServer systems, Digital
is setting a new standard by bundling in three years of hardware warranty.
In addition, Digital is offering a competitive level of software warranty
coverage on all operating systems and bundled NAS products at 90 days
conformance to SPD, with advisory telephone support.

The only exception is the DEC 7000 Model 700. It will carry a one-year
onsite, 5 x 9, four hour response hardware warranty (i.e., DECservice) with
system installation included. The software warranty is set for one year with
telephone advisory and remedial support, critical onsite support, Advanced
Electronic Support, and rights to new versions.

The DEC 7000 Model 700 hardware warranty may be upgraded from one year to
three years with an extended warranty. There are no service part numbers to
upgrade the DEC 7000 Model 700 warranty.

Note: In this article, 5 x 9, 5 x 12, 6 x 16, and 7 x 24 denote the days and
the hours of warranty service. For example, 5 x 9 corresponds to 5 days a
week (Monday through Friday), 9 hours a day (8 a.m. to 5 p.m.) that service
is available.

Warranty for AlphaStation 200 and 400

For the new AlphaStation 200 and 400 system products, the standard warranty
attributes are as follows:

o  Hardware -- Three year: First year onsite, next day response, 5 x 9
   coverage. Parts and labor included. Second and third year:
   Return-to-Digital via carry-in to a Digital Servicenter or mail in.
   Digital will repair or replace within 48 hours of receipt.

o  All Operating Systems -- 90 day, conformance to SPD, advisory telephone
   support. (Note: DEC OSF/1 configurations that include Open 3D and
   Multimedia Services, as well as OpenVMS configurations with Open 3D, will
   carry the same level of software warranty for these other bundled
   software products.)

o  NAS 150: 90 day, conformance to SPD, advisory telephone support.

Users who require a higher level of support during the warranty period
should consider Supplemental Service Packages. (See Supplemental Services
section for more details.)

Warranty for AlphaServer 1000, 2000, and 2100

The new AlphaServer systems carry the following warranty attributes:

o  Hardware: Three years onsite, next day response, 5 x 9 coverage. Parts
   and labor included.

o  All operating systems: 90 day, conformance to SPD, advisory telephone
   support.

o  NAS 200: 90 day, conformance to SPD, advisory telephone support.

Users who require a higher level of support during the warranty period
should consider Supplemental Service Packages. (See Supplemental Services
section for more details.)

The New Software Warranty

In the past, Digital has provided telephone support on software warranty
that included advisory and remedial attributes when purchased at standard
price. The new warranty no longer includes remedial content or the rights to
new versions. Digital has added easy to order Supplemental Services to
better match the varying needs of both users and business partners.

The new Software Warranty includes the following key features:

o  90 days conformance to SPD.
o  90 days advisory telephone support, available Monday through Friday, 8:00
   a.m. to 5:00 p.m. This includes information on product features and usage
   questions, advisory support on installation, and advisory support on
   problem isolation and notification.

Advisory telephone support includes software usage advice on proper software
execution and information on the interpretation of software product
technical documentation. It also includes advice on the proper installation
and updates of user installable software. The installation support is
limited to getting the user started and answering specific questions
encountered during the installation process.

Advisory support also includes problem isolation. Digital will determine
whether a software usage problem is the result of a hardware failure or
software problem. Problem notification support includes notifying the
appropriate software organization or vendor of any unpublished software
usage problems. This support does not include any onsite software support or
guaranteed problem resolution. It does not include any call response time
guarantees or telephone call backs. Electronic problem submission and
electronic conferencing are available through Supplemental Service upgrades.
Advisory telephone support is provided Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to
5:00 p.m.

Software Warranty can be enhanced with supplemental software support
options. The key features are:

DEC OSF/1 or OpenVMS System	      Windows NT System
Packaged Software                     Packaged Software

o  1 or 3 year options		      o	 1 or 3 year options
o  Advisory and Remedial	      o	 Advisory and Remedial
   Software Support (7 x 24)	      	 Software Support (7 x 24)
o  Rights to new versions
o  Advanced Electronic Support
o  Critical Onsite Support

(See the Supplemental Services section of this article for more details and
ordering information.)

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The new warranty and supplemental service offerings for AlphaStation and
AlphaServer systems are available now. The U.S. List and Standard price are
now equal, with three years of warranty embedded. Also, please note that
these part numbers are inclusive of any in-cabinet factory installed options
(e.g., incremental memory, disks, and network cards) that are ordered and
shipped with the new system.

These part number are not applicable for Europe and the Asia Pacific area.
For details on supplemental services in these areas, please contact the
local Digital Service representative.

Hardware Supplemental Services

There are two types of supplemental service upgrades for the AlphaStation
systems. The first package upgrades from the one year, 5 x 9, onsite with
next day response and two year return to Digital warranty to a three year, 5
x 9, onsite with next day service response.

The second supplemental service upgrade for the AlphaStation system upgrades
from the one year, 5 x 9, onsite with next day response and two year return
to Digital warranty to a three year onsite warranty with four hour
guaranteed response time and options for 5 x 9, 5 x 12, 6 x 16, and 7 x 24
call windows.

The AlphaServer system supplemental service packages will upgrade the three
year warranty from 5 x 9, next day service to a four hour guaranteed
response time, with options for 5 x 9, 5 x 12, 6 x 16, and 7 x 24 call
windows.

