ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES for New AlphaStation and AlphaServer Products

HIGHLIGHTS

o  New upgrades available to all new AlphaStation and AlphaServer systems

o  Trade-in amount embedded in trade-in upgrade price

o  Retain the old system onsite for 60 days before returning to Digital

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION

In conjunction with the new Alpha products, Digital is expanding its
ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE program to include upgrades from older Digital systems to
these new product offerings. Refer to the new Alpha product announcements in
this issue for specific product detail.

Alpha Enterprise Servers

The new DEC 7000 Model 700 system gives greater CPU performance than its
predecessor, the DEC 7000 Model 600 system, by using the 275 MHz Alpha CPU.
There are two types of ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES available:

o  Simple board upgrades from the DEC 7000 and DEC 10000 AXP or VAX 7000 and
   VAX 10000 systems.

o  Trade-in (system replacement) upgrades for VAX 64xx, 65xx, and 66xx.

Alpha Departmental Servers

The AlphaServer family has now been extended with smaller configurations and
the use of the EV45 275 MHz Alpha CPU. The user now can choose from the:

o  AlphaServer 2100 4/275.
o  AlphaServer 2100 4/200 (originally named Digital 2100 Server A500MP).
o  AlphaServer 2000 4/200.

Two types of ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES will be available for departmental servers:

o  Board upgrades from today's Digital 2100 Server A500MP.

o  Trade-in upgrades (system replacements) for VAX, DECsystem, and older
   Alpha systems.

Alpha WorkGroup Servers

The new entry-level Alpha server is the AlphaServer 1000 4/200. The
ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES available for workgroup servers are trade-in (system
replacement) upgrades from MicroVAX, VAX 4100, DEC 3000, and DEC 2000
systems.

Alpha Workstations

The new workstations, the AlphaStation 400 4/233, the AlphaStation 200
4/166, and the AlphaStation 200 4/233 add extra performance, broaden the
product line, and introduce the PCI bus to the Alpha workstation family.

The ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES available for workstations consist of trade-in
(workstation replacement) upgrades from selected DECstation, VAXstation, and
Alpha workstations.

BENEFITS

o  Improved cost of ownership -- what the payback period could be.

o  The maintenance savings of replacing old disk technology with
   StorageWorks software.

o  Digital's new software licensing policies mean low software upgrade
   costs, preserving the user's previous software investment.

o  Ease of doing an upgrade.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The ADVANTAGE-UPGRADES for the new Alpha workstations and servers are
available with product availability. In Europe, for some ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE
offerings, there is a special European-wide program that does not use these
upgrade part numbers.

Refer to the November Systems and Options Catalog for the latest upgrade
information and configurations.

