PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DEC FUSE for DEC OSF/1 AXP Systems is a DEC OSF/1 Motif workstation-based
programming environment that runs on DEC OSF/1 V2.0 and V3.0 AXP systems.
The DEC FUSE environment contains integrated graphical user interfaces
(GUIs) to commonly used UNIX programming tools and utilities, editors, and
program source browsers. The dynamic, mouse-sensitive graphical tools
greatly simplify the tasks of navigating within programs and identifying
problems.

DEC FUSE supports programmers and programming work groups that are not
necessarily UNIX experts. With the help of its graphical user interface,
programmers can learn about the capabilities of UNIX utilities without
having to memorize commands and options. DEC FUSE also appeals to
programmers who are already familiar with UNIX and want an integrated suite
of graphical tools rather than terminal-based, command-line oriented tools.

BENEFITS

o  The new distributed build capabilities enable users to distribute a build
   across hosts (including non-Alpha AXP hosts) on a LAN, increasing the use
   of available system resources.

o  The builder can use existing makefiles or create new ones. DEC FUSE
   graphically displays the module dependencies, showing out of date modules
   through color-coding. Integration between editors and the builder speeds
   error correction.

o  The new Compare tool provides a GUI to the UNIX diff utility. Through
   integration with the Code Manager, users can display differences between
   file revisions in both SCCS and RCS libraries.

