File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems V1.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Reliable file transfer capability between heterogeneous systems using
   TCP/IP

o  Available for DEC OSF/1 AXP, OpenVMS VAX and AXP, HP-UX (HP9000, 700 and
   800 series) and IBM AS/400 platforms

o  Error recovery and automatic restart

o  Same user interface provided for all platforms

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems V1.0 is a software application
offering automatic, reliable, and scheduled file transfers between
heterogeneous systems. The file transfers can be queued and occur in
background mode, allowing the user to continue to perform other tasks. The
File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems (SPD 54.34) uses the standard TCP/IP
and FTP protocols. It can tranfer ASCII, binary, and EBCDIC (AS/400 only)
files depending on the File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems operation mode
used -- Normal, Basic, or FTP mode.

In Normal Mode, the File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems provides a
checkpointing mechanism so that whenever a copy operation fails due to
network link failures or other similar errors, the copy operation will pause
and restart from the point of failure, at a later time, thus wisely using
network resources.

Features

o  Reliable file transfer capability between heterogeneous systems using
   TCP/IP
o  Automatic file transfers
o  Scheduled file transfers
o  Access control on remote host system (mechanism based on username and
   password authentication)
o  Programmable recovery
o  Post-transfer commands
o  Job history
o  User notification
o  File transfer abort
o  Easy user interface
o  Alias name: a remote alias name can be used in place of the full Remote
   Node Access File information
o  Remote TCP/IP systems support: In either FTP or Basic Mode, File Transfer
   Spooler for Open Systems can transfer files between a local File Transfer
   Spooler for Open Systems and remote systems that are running only TCP/IP
   -- such as UNIX based systems, MS-DOS, and generally any system capable
   of running FTP

File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems differs from File Transfer Spooler
for OpenVMS Systems in that the latter uses DECnet protocol, and File
Transfer Spooler for Open Systems uses FTP and TCP/IP, and can run on
different heterogeneous platforms. In addition, File Transfer Spooler for
OpenVMS Systems V3.0 has a compression algorithm that is not currently
available for File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems.

Performance for the File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems depends entirely
upon the base FTP performance of the network, which varies from case to
case.

A licence is required for each node. A protocol runs on each machine to
segment the file; File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems must be installed
on both sides to allow a restart at the point of failure. However, the retry
mechanism works even if File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems is not
installed on the remote system. File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems can
send files to a remote node that only has FTP, in which case the user
benefits from the common user interface and scheduling, but the retry is
performed on the complete file instead of restarting from point of failure
within the file.

Copy commands are subset functions of File Transfer Spooler for Open
Systems, which also provides recoverability, schedulability, and various
other features.

BENEFITS

o  Reduces communications costs.
o  Provides reliable file transfer.
o  Provides a simple and common user interface between different systems.

The transfer of files in a heterogeneous environment is often limited by the
lack of common transport mechanisms. One of the most common standards is
TCP/IP with FTP. Because FTP has no automatic restart mechanism, any failure
results in a manual and complete restart -- which can have very high
telecommunications and organizational costs.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems is available now through
Digital's sales offices and Professional Services Centers.

