TECHNICAL DATA

File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems is implemented in three modes:

o  In Normal Mode (used for transferring ASCII files between two File
   Transfer Spoolers for Open Systems) File Transfer Spooler for Open
   Systems:
   - Checks the availability of space on the target system before a copy
     takes place.
   - Uses a temporary file name for the destination file before a complete
     and successful file tranfer.
   - Uses an error recovery and restart mechanism in the event of file
     transfer failures, allowing the file to be transferred later from the
     point where the error occurred.

o  In Basic Mode (used for transferring ASCII, binary, and EBCDIC -- AS/400
   only -- files between a local system and a remote system with file
   formats incompatible with the Normal Mode), File Transfer Spooler for
   Open Systems uses:
   - A temporary file name for the destination file.
   - An error recovery and restart mechanism allowing a file to be fully
   transferred later.

o  In FTP Mode (for transferring files from a local system to a remote
   system using FTP), File Transfer Spooler for Open Systems:
   - Transfers ASCII, binary, and EBCDIC (AS/400 only) source files directly
     to the destination files.
   - Uses an error recovery and restart mechanism allowing a file to be
     fully transferred later.

Hardware and Software Required

o  Any VAX system running OpenVMS V5.5-2 or higher, and DEC TCP/IP Services
