POLYCENTER Save Set Manager V1.0 for OpenVMS VAX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Up to 50 percent reduction in time spent on backup/restore operations
   without compromising data integrity

o  Transfer of backup save sets between tape drive technologies

o  Reduction in downtime for an OpenVMS backup/restore operation

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The POLYCENTER Save Set Manager V1.0 for OpenVMS (SPD 62.64.01) is a layered
software product that reduces operational time during OpenVMS backup
activities by providing offline save set validation, copy, and merge
functions.

The amount of data users must back up is growing exponentially. At the same
time, global business needs are shrinking the available time many users have
to perform their backups. Digital's user surveys have consistently shown a
high need for products that help users deal with the "shrinking backup
window." Users with aging, low capacity media need tools to transfer their
backup data onto modern, high capacity, high integrity media -- and remove
the aging systems and devices required to support the old media.

BENEFITS

o  Reduction of operational time spent on online backup and restore without
   compromising data integrity.
o  Selective manipulation of save set contents and attributes.
o  Transfer of backup save sets between tape drive technologies.
o  Copy of backup save sets from one tape or disk drive to another tape or
   disk drive while maintaining data integrity.
o  Reduced downtime for a backup/restore operation.
o  Ability to monitor degradation of archived save sets.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The POLYCENTER Save Set Manager for OpenVMS software is available now
through Digital's sales offices, DECdirect and Electronic Store services,
and business partners.

A special introductory price per node will be available until December 31,
1994.

