TLZ07 4mm Digital Audio Tape Drive

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides up to 8 Gbyte capacity

o  Ideal for unattended backup of workstations and servers

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DDS-2 compliant TLZ07 tape drive provides up to 8 Gbytes of unattended
backup and archiving capability, with a transfer rate of up to 810 Kbytes
per second. This new Digital Audio Tape (DAT) product is read/write
compatible with the media used in the TLZ06 and TLZ6L loader and the TLZ04.

BENEFITS

The introduction of the TLZ07 represents the next step forward in the
capabilities of 4mm Digital Audio Tape products. Benefits include:

o  High unattended backup capacity -- The DDS-2 format provides a native
   unattended capacity 4 Gbytes and compressed capacity of 8 Gbytes,
   providing an effective match for many of today's small servers.

o  First generation read/write compatibility -- The TLZ07 can read and write
   both DDS-2 and DDS-1 media, ensuring investment protection as well as
   data interchange with DDS-1 drives.

o  Multiple packaging options -- The TLZ07 is available in system-installed,
   tabletop, and StorageWorks versions, enabling widespread use and
   convenience. A loader version is being considered to provide both
   tabletop and StorageWorks variants.

o  Media quality checking -- The TLZ07 implements the new DDS-2 media
   recognition system, eliminating performance and service issues related to
   use of audio-grade media cartridges.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TLZ07 tape drive will be available in the U.S. in late October, and
outside the U.S. in mid November through local Digital sales offices and
business partners.

