DECwanrouter 90 ISDN Offers Fully Integrated Solution

HIGHLIGHTS

o  New integrated ISDN basic rate port

o  ISDN dial-on-demand and automatic ISDN backup of the serial line

o  FLASH memory for fast software restart

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DECwanrouter 90 ISDN (Integrated Services Digital Networks) is a fully
integrated solution for ISDN networks. The DECwanrouter 90 ISDN is a
multiprotocol router, providing routing support for TCP/IP, Novell NetWare
(IPX), DECnet (Phase IV and V), and OSI host systems.

Providing two independent B-channels at 64 Kbits per second each, the
DECwanrouter 90 ISDN has the capability of automatically establishing or
disconnecting ISDN circuits, maintaining a connection only when real data is
being sent over the network. The use of this ISDN dynamic mechanism provides
a low cost internetworking solution for remote offices. Another key feature
is the capability of automatically backing up the traffic over the serial
port with an ISDN circuit. The DECwanrouter 90 ISDN also supports
synchronous and asynchronous communications at various speeds -- up to 64
Kbits per second on the additional serial port.

For optimum flexibility, the DECwanrouter 90 ISDN is supplied either as a
standalone unit, or as a DEChub 90 or 900 module.

BENEFITS

o  Use of cost effective ISDN services for internetworking solution either
   for primary use or for secondary use as a leased line circuit backup.

o  FLASH memory to eliminate software downline loading.

o  PC loading and management for site only having PCs.

o  Novell IPX routing for NetWare environments.

o  Interoperability with DECNIS.

