DECnet/OSI V3.0 for DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides connectivity and interoperability with other Digital Network
   Architecture (DNA) Phase IV and Phase V implementations

o  Supports DEC OSF/1 V3.0 features such as SMP

o  Now holds up to 100,000 addresses in an expanded local network database

o  Provides wide area networking support via X.25 V1.1 for DEC OSF/1 systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECnet/OSI V3.0 for DEC OSF/1 software provides DECnet plus OSI network
protocols and their applications to systems running V3.0 of the DEC OSF/1
operating system.

DECnet/OSI for DEC OSF/1 software supports communications with any DNA Phase
IV and Phase V implementations including DECnet-VAX, DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS
VAX and AXP, DECnet/OSI for ULTRIX, DECnet for OpenVMS AXP, and PATHWORKS
software.

The DECnet/OSI V3.0 for DEC OSF/1 end system license provides the following
set of DECnet and OSI protocols and services:

o  Ethernet 802.3 and Token Ring 802.5 connectivity as well as large packet
   FDDI support for high performance networking.
o  OSI addressing that supports connectivity to computer networks with
   millions of nodes.
o  Local and global directory service options.
o  CLNP over HDLC for point-to-point support.
o  DECdts network time service (client and server) for synchronizing time
   among distributed systems.
o  DECnet-Internet gateway for DECnet and TCP/IP interoperability.
o  OSI File Transfer, Access, and Management (FTAM); and Virtual Terminal
   (VT) applications.
o  DECnet/OSI over X.25 using LLC2/CONS protocol.

The DECnet/OSI extended function license includes all of the above, plus:
o  An FTAM to FTP (TCP/IP file transfer protocol) gateway.
o  Virtual Terminal gateways for VT/Telnet, VT/CTERM, and LAT to VT.

For additional WAN networking requirements, X.25 V1.1 for DEC OSF/1 systems
provides X.25 connectivity and wide area device drivers. Refer to the X.25
V1.1 for DEC OSF/1 systems article in this issue for additional information.

New Features

o  Segregated routing mode -- This settable attribute will direct the
   routing layer to choose a DNA Phase IV router for packets with a
   destination address that can be translated to the Phase IV format.

o  Enhanced directory service options -- DECnet/OSI software provides simple
   access to the node name and addressing information stored in one or more
   directory services. With V3.0, two options are supported:
   - Local -- Stores names and address information locally in database
     files; up to 100,000 addresses may be stored locally.
   - Distributed -- Stores names and address information in Digital
     Distributed Name Service (server software available for OpenVMS VAX and
     ULTRIX systems), a global directory service.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECnet/OSI V3.0 for DEC OSF/1 is available now.

Media and Documentation

The software kit will be supplied on the December 1994 DEC OSF/1 Layered
Product CD-ROM. Hardcopy documents are also available. The new features of
DECnet/OSI V3.0 for DEC OSF/1 are documented in the Release Notes.

Until the Layered Product CD-ROM ships, licensed users will be provided with
network copies of the kit. For information on how to obtain this kit,
contact your local Digital sales representative or business partner.

