DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Support for DEC OSF/1 as management and load hosts

o  Support for TCP/IP based networking connectivity

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 is a member of Digital's family of DEC SNA
network transport products. This family consists of hardware and software
products that connect suitably configured Digital networked systems to IBM
systems in a Systems Network Architecture (SNA) environment. When DEC SNA
products are used with the appropriate OpenVMS, ULTRIX, DEC OSF/1, Microsoft
Windows, or MS-DOS access routines, users can exchange information and share
resources between Digital and IBM networked systems.

The DEC SNA Domain Gateway software (SPD 38.69.xx) addresses SNA networked
3270 and PC connectivity to:

o  Standard off the shelf OpenVMS VAX applications that normally run on a VT
   terminal -- This is achieved using the DEC SNA Domain Gateway product in
   conjunction with the MEP VT for DEC SNA 3270 Application Services.

o  OpenVMS VAX DECforms applications -- This is done through the blockmode
   support of 3270 terminals that is built into DECforms.

o  Custom OpenVMS VAX applications -- The applications are written using the
   DEC SNA 3270 Applications Programming Interface.

o  Custom DEC OSF/1 applications -- The applications are written using the
   DEC SNA 3270 Applications Progamming Interface.

Used with the DEC SNA 3270 Application Services Print Symbiont, the DEC SNA
Domain Gateway V2.0 also provides the ability to print from OpenVMS VAX
systems to SNA networked printers.

DEC SNA Domain Gateway software is part of both Digital and IBM SNA
networks. Architecturally, it is a DECnet/OSI end node to a DECnet network;
and an IP end node (RFC 1122), Physical Unit Type 5 (PU T5) node to SNA. The
DEC SNA Domain Gateway product appears to the SNA network as an SNA Domain
system that contains one subarea. The software provides bi-directional
access between Digital and IBM SNA networks.

Connecting directly to an Ethernet LAN and an IBM S/370 Block Mutiplexer
channel or IBM front end processor, the SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 provides SNA
connectivity to any Digital supported DECnet/OSI or DECnet Phase IV system
in the DECnet network, and any TCP/IP based system in the IP network.

Because DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 is a PU T5 implementation, it enables
DECnet/OSI or TCP/IP based applications to be either Primary Logical Units
(PLUs) or Secondary Logical Units (SLUs) when communicating with IBM
applications and peripheral devices. This means that suitably configured
Digital-based applications can be interactively accessed from IBM SNA
networked 3270 devices and PCs. The 3270 connectivity to applications is
achieved using the DEC SNA Domain Gateway in conjunction with DEC SNA 3270
Application Services and MEP VT for DEC SNA 3270 Application Services
products.

NOTE: If DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 will run on a DEC OSF/1 system without
      DECnet/OSI installed, it cannot be configured for DECnet software. In
      a TCP/IP only environment, the software can only be configured for
      TCP/IP. If the DEC OSF/1 system runs DECnet software, DEC SNA Domain
      Gateway V2.0 can be configured for DECnet software, TCP/IP, or both.
      With an OpenVMS VAX system running DECnet/OSI, the product can be
      configured for TCP/IP.

New Features

o  DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 adds support for Alpha systems running the
   DEC OSF/1 operating system with prerequisite software for managing and
   downline loading Domain Gateway software.

o  DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 adds support for TCP/IP based networking
   protocols. The software can now be configured to operate as a DECnet/OSI
   end node, TCP/IP end node, or gateway supporting both DECnet/OSI and
   TCP/IP.

o  The DEC OSF/1 Kit for DEC SNA Domain Gateway V2.0 contains a tn3270
   server that allows any tn3270 client to connect via the tn3270 server to
   an IBM mainframe, without requiring that mainframe to run TCP/IP.

