X.25 V1.1 for DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  X.25 support for DEC OSF/1 V3.0 systems

o  ISDN port on DEC 3000 systems supported

o  Permanent Virtual Circuits supported

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

New Alpha systems that require DEC OSF/1 V3.0 now support wide area
networking. With the availability of X.25 V1.1 (SPD 42.47), users can
connect these new Alpha systems to X.25 Packet-Switching Data Networks
(PSDNs). In addition, those with DEC 3000 systems can take advantage of
low-cost, high performance ISDN Basic Rate Access lines for wide area
connections.

X.25 for DEC OSF/1 systems is a layered software product that enables
appropriately configured DEC OSF/1 systems to connect to an X.25 Packet
Switched Data Network (PSDN) as client to an X.25 Relay node on the same
local area network (LAN), as an X.25 relay node, or directly via a
synchronous communications link.

The product provides further software, enabling DEC 3000 systems to connect
directly to a supported Integrated Services Digital Network (ISDN). Only the
single line Basic Rate Access (BRA) interface of the DEC 3000 AXP systems is
supported.

X.25 V1.1 for DEC OSF/1 systems supports communications via PSDNs conforming
to CCITT recommendation X.25 1980, 1984, and 1988 or to international
standard ISO 8208. (Refer to SPD 42.47 for a list of supported PSDNs and
ISDNs.)

X.25 for DEC OSF/1 allows an Alpha system to:

o  Act as a packet-mode DTE connected to a supported PSDN.
o  Support ISO 8208 DTE to DTE point-to-point operation.
o  Act as a packet-mode DTE connected to a LAN.
o  Act as an X.25 relay node conforming to ISO Technical Report 10029.
o  Provide an X.25 subnetwork for DECnet/OSI CONS and CLNS operation.
o  Provide a DEC-HDLC point-to-point data link for DECnet/OSI CLNS
   operation.
o  Act as a functional TE connected at reference point "S" to a supported
   ISDN.
o  Connect to a supported PSDN Access Unit via a circuit switched ISDN
   B-Channel.
o  Act as a combination of the above.

The following functions are supported by X.25 V1.1:

o  X.25 relay per ISO TR10029
o  DECnet/OSI connectionless network service
o  DECnet/OSI connection oriented network service
o  TCP/IP over X.25 per RFC1356
o  TCP/IP over ISDN using the Point to Point Protocol (PPP)
o  X.25 and higher layers over circuit switched ISDN
o  Process-to-process (X.25 network service) communication
o  Process-to-terminal (X.29) communication
o  Terminal-to-process (X.29) communication
o  X.25 mail

New Features

o  Support for DEC OSF/1 V3.0 features such as symmetric multiprocessing
o  Support for permanent virtual circuits
o  Support for single line Basic Rate Access (BRA) to ISDN for DEC 3000 AXP
   systems

With this release, on DEC 3000 AXP systems an ISDN circuit switched
B-channel can be used to transport TCP/IP traffic using the Point to Point
Protocol (PPP) in accordance with internet RFC-1331.

ISDN circuit switched B-channel access is supported to a PSDN Access Unit
(AU). This allows X.25 traffic over an ISDN connection. All functionality
supported for X.25 switched virtual circuits is then available over the ISDN
link. This functionality also allows two end nodes to communicate using X.25
in a DTE to DTE configuration over an ISDN circuit switched B-channel.

Management of the ISDN interface is handled by user utilities based around
the standard TCP/IP model, with an /etc/isdn.hosts database used to manage
all information required to make and receive ISDN calls from remote systems.

Problem solving is facilitated by the provision of the Common Trace Facility
(CTF) which enables trace and analysis of both X.25 traffic and ISDN
D-Channel activity.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

X.25 V1.1 for DEC OSF/1 systems is available now. The software kit will be
supplied on the December 1994 DEC OSF/1 Layered Product CD-ROM. Hard copy
documents also are available. New features for this release of X.25 for DEC
OSF/1 systems have been documented in the Release Notes.

Until the Layered Product CD-ROM ships, licensed users will be provided with
network copies of the kit. For information on how to obtain this kit,
contact your local Digital sales representative or business partner.

