RUMBA Tools Accelerate Development of Client/Server Applications

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Add new functions

o  Give legacy applications a graphical front-end

o  Develop an entire new system of client/server applications in record time

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Software developers can renew a host system in just weeks, not months, and
cut application development costs when they team RUMBA software with RUMBA
tools (SPD 63.09). With these award-winning tools, users can change the
workflow, add new functions, and give legacy applications a graphical
front-end, or develop a whole new system of client/server applications in
record time.

o  RUMBA Tools for Visual Basic -- Streamlines application development in
   the Visual Basic environment, allowing users to create new graphical
   front-ends for legacy applications on IBM mainframes, AS/400, or
   Digital's VAX or Alpha systems easily. It also enables the development of
   new APPC applications without writing a single line of APPC code. This
   complete, flexible tool lets users work the way they want. Users can call
   EHLLAPI or APPC functions directly, or use functions from the RUMBA
   Developer Library to make development simpler. Visual Basic source code
   is included, so functions can be customized or converted into different
   languages, such as C or Cobol, as desired.

   For even easier development, users can employ RUMBA custom controls. They
   look and work just like familiar Visual Basic controls, but have been
   enhanced with RUMBA specific properties and events. Easier still, the
   QuickBuilder utility translates host screens in seconds. With just a
   mouse click, QuickBuilder translates specified host screen fields, menus,
   function keys, and data into RUMBA custom controls. Options are provided
   for setting colors, fonts, and styles before building the form. Users can
   add icons and other finishing touches as desired.

o  RUMBA Tools for EHLLAPI -- This is the easy way to develop and install
   custom graphical interfaces for existing or new host applications. Users
   get the full set of standard IBM EHLLAPI function calls in simpler form,
   several additional calls for accessing RUMBA software's powerful
   connectivity features, and more. RUMBA Tools for EHLLAPI supports EHLLAPI
   function calls from both DOS and Windows. The Dynamic Link Library
   contains EHLLAPI function calls in both IBM EHLLAPI and WD Equivalent
   Function formats. EHLLAPI programming guidelines, instructions for using
   EHALLPI calls, sample programs, and extensive online help also are
   provided.

o  RUMBA Tools for DDE -- These tools provide a full set of DDE messages,
   diagnostics, and sample programs that show users how to use DDE to
   exchange data between the host and Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Word for
   Windows, or a DDE-enabled Windows application. The DDE Message Library
   contains all the messages needed to establish a conversation between the
   application and RUMBA software, pass keystrokes, and commands to the
   host, and receive data in return. The Library supports any language that
   can make DDE calls, including Windows, C, Visual Basic, Pascal, and Macro
   language applications. Users also get the SDK Trace Utility, which allows
   them to monitor conversations between DDE applications and RUMBA software
   interactively.

o  RUMBA Tools for APPC -- These tools save application developers weeks of
   effort implementing APPC and CPI-C applications. The exclusive RUMBA
   CPI-CEasy API reduces APPC application development to four simple
   function calls. VerbTalk, a powerful APPC macro scripting utility, lets
   users point and click buttons to include APPC verbs or condition
   statements in the macro. FastPath lets users configure their APPC
   sessions in seconds. The Trace utility allows users to monitor
   conversations between transaction programs interactively to shortcut
   troubleshooting. APPN End Node support is also provided.

o  RUMBA Tools for PowerBuilder -- These simplify the development of
   graphical front-ends and APPC/CPI-C client/server applications in the
   PowerBuilder environment. Its enhanced User Objects tightly integrate
   host data with the PowerBuilder application, so less coding and no
   EHLLAPI experience is required. A robust set of EHLLAPI calls are
   conveniently bundled in PowerScript routines for easy implementation.
   Sample EHLLAPI PowerScript programs are included along with complete
   documentation that demonstrates all EHLLAPI functions in PowerScript
   syntax. Users also get a comprehensive set of DDE messages to establish
   dynamic data links between PowerBuilder applications and host data, and a
   sample DDE PowerScript program to get started.

o  RUMBA Graphics for Digital -- This brings VAX, Alpha, and UNIX VT340
   system graphics to desktop PCs, where users can work with them in the
   friendly, intuitive Windows environment, with no more arcane codes and
   difficult displays. With simple mouse clicks users can connect to the
   host or server they want to access, display the desired directory, select
   a file, and get down to work fast. Users can recolor graphics with the
   256-color palette, resize graphic windows while running, iconize, and
   restore the file with a mouse click, and more. Users can run multiple
   graphic sessions or a combination of graphics and other host or server
   sessions simultaneously from a single VAX system, from multiple VAX,
   Alpha, and UNIX systems, and from Windows desktop applications. All
   ReGIS, Sixel, and TEKTRONIX 4010/4014 graphics are supported. RUMBA
   Graphics for Digital works with RUMBA OFFICE for Digital and RUMBA for
   Digital Hosts products.

o  RUMBA Graphics, Mainframe Edition -- This tool makes IBM mainframe
   graphics as easy to work with as a favorite Windows or OS/2 graphics
   package. Users can cut and paste mainframe graphics into Windows or OS/2
   applications, edit graphic elements and text, save images to file or
   print, and more. RUMBA Graphics supports IBM AS, IBM Interactive Chart
   Utility, SAS/GRAPH, Telegraf, and other IBM GDDM all points addressable
   (APA) graphics. It also supports programmed symbol graphics. RUMBA
   Graphics, Mainframe Edition works with RUMBA OFFICE for Digital, and
   RUMBA for Digital, Mainframe Edition products.

