DEC ACB V2.2 for OpenVMS

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Facilitates the secure connection to an OpenVMS system from a terminal or
   PC

o  V2.2 supports OpenVMS AXP and DECnet/OSI software, additional system
   management and accounting commands, and updated MS-DOS and Windows
   clients

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DEC ACB software is a management utility that facilitates the secure
connection to an OpenVMS VAX or AXP system from a terminal or a PC. Users
can access a host system running DEC ACB software directly, or they can
supply a phone number on which DEC ACB will call the user back and start the
required session. Users can be validated by the local DEC ACB system or on a
remote DEC ACB system running the Remote Authentication Interface Server.
(This latter option is available only in a DECnet network.)

Users are authenticated based on a random challenge and response, which
protects the system from replay attacks. The password is automatically
changed at each connection, creating a secure system that requires minimal
password management, and which renders line tapping ineffective.

V2.2 Features

o  Supports OpenVMS AXP platforms.

o  Supports DECnet/OSI software (exception: DEC ACB does not support
   DECnet/OSI for asynchronous communications).

o  Checks at login for remaining connection time.

o  Supports Security Dynamics Authentication Token with optional
   installation of ACM/5100 software.

o  Includes new system management commands such as: SHUT ACB, SET CALLBACK,
   and SET HOME_NODE.

o  Provides new qualifiers for SET ACCESS_HOURS: /STRICT and /NOSTRICT.

o  Includes numerous enhancements, including a new screen interface for PC
   clients and improved authentication.

o  Includes pricing and licensing modifications.

BENEFITS

o  Extension of support to OpenVMS AXP and DECnet/OSI software provides more
   computing options for users.

o  Numerous additions and enhancements to system management commands provide
   more flexible and secure usage.

o  It is easier to control the connection time, maximizing the availability
   of the system and control over individual users.

o  More choice in the user authentication options provide better protection
   from unauthorized use.

o  Availability of the Application Programming Interface provides easier
   product extensibility.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DEC ACB V2.2 is available now.

