TECHNICAL DATA

o  Protocol support
   - Dialup terminal lines.
   - X.29 incoming connections.
   - LAT connections to OpenVMS VAX computers.
   - Any type of interactive access to an OpenVMS VAX or AXP system (except
     DECwindows login).

o  Types of sessions supported
   - Interactive: the local system username prompt is displayed.
   - LAT: The user can access a DECserver Emulator (VTLAT), providing
     simultaneous connections up to 12 LAT services.
   - DECnet session: an asynchronous DDCMP connection is started on the
     current active connection, (only valid on Asynchronous communications
     controllers and DECnet Phase IV).
   - Telnet: the user has access to the Telnet utility and can connect to
     host systems on a TCP/IP network.
   - DEC MAILworks session: the DEC MAILworks CTI broker is automatically
     invoked. Possible connection to a host system via MS-DOS MAILworks
     client or TeamLinks for Windows software.

o  Hardware requirements
   - Any VAX or AXP system with a minimum of 0.9 VUPS CPU capacity.
   - One or more asynchronous modems connected to a telephone network and
     supporting an Automatic Dialing Unit protocol such as the AT command
     set, DMCL, or a protocol that complies with the V.25bis CCITT
     recommendation.
   - One or more asynchronous communication systems: 802.3 Ethernet terminal
     server, DECserver 200/MC, 700-16, 700-08, or 550 with CXY08-Ax option,
     or BI/Q-bus/Unibus controllers with full modem control such as DMB32,
     DHB32 (with CK-DHB32-Ax cabinet Kit), CXY08, DHQ11, DHV11, DHU11,
     DMF32, port 0 and 1, and DMZ32 (with CK-DMZ32-AY cabinet kit).
   - One or more asynchronous communication cables (BC22EE-xx, BC22F-xx).
     Optionally, BC23C-01 for terminal server connection.

o  Optional hardware
   - Any synchronous device supported by VAX PSI V4.3 or later for incoming
     X.29 access control.
   - For optional user authentication: IBM compatible PC, RACAL Watchword
     Generator, Security Dynamics authentication token (available directly
     from Racal Datacom and Security Dynamics).

o  Software requirements
   - OpenVMS VAX V5.5 and later or OpenVMS AXP V6.1 and later.

o  Optional software
   - DECnet Phase IV.
   - DECnet/OSI software.
   - DECmcc V1.2 or later (for optional DECmcc reporting).
   - VAX PSI V4.3 or later or VAX PSI-ACCESS V4.3 or later for incoming X.29
     access control.
   - ACM/5100 is required for SecurID authentication, available directly
     from Security Dynamics.

o  Optional software for PC-based authentication systems
   - MS-DOS V3.3 or later (for the MS-DOS PC client).
   - Windows V3.1 or later (for the Windows PC client).
   - Terminal emulation software for MS-DOS or Windows (for example, Kermit,
     SETHOST, and the built-in terminal utility in Windows).
   - DEC MAILworks software for DOS V1.1 or later.

SERVICES

